  - name: "The Bestowed Transformation"
    description: "Printed 95, and ONLY for a bestowed character. The person is normal in every way until he calls on the power within - by force of will, by naming the bestowing power, or by a trigger word - and is instantly transformed into a mighty costumed visage of power. A child, an old man or an invalid becomes a youthful, powerfully built heroic figure. While transformed: M.A. +2D6 to a minimum of 18, P.S. +2D6 to a minimum of 20, P.P. +1D6 to a minimum of 18, Speed multiplied by 2D4 to a minimum of 24, and +2D4x10 S.D.C. I.Q., M.E. and P.E. are unchanged. These apply ONLY while transformed, which is why they are not on the class."
extraction_notes: "THE S.D.C. IS A BASE OF 20 PLUS A TOP-UP ON THE CHOSEN PACKAGE, and the arithmetic is the book''s: printed 90 gives the magic weapon wielder 20, printed 91 the enchanted object wielder 35, printed 92 the wizard 30, printed 95 the magician 30 and the mystically bestowed 20. A variant CAN override `sdc_base` and an ability CANNOT, but an ability is where the power block has to live - `VARIANT_OVERRIDES` carries no `magic` and no `super_abilities` - so putting the S.D.C. on the ability as a pool bonus keeps the whole decision in ONE pick. The variants carry the sub-type name and nothing else. THE SIXTEEN OPTIONS ARE A FLATTENED TREE. The book rolls twice: once for the source of the magic, and again on that source''s own table - six outcomes for an enchanted object and seven for a bestowed character. Nothing here can gate one choice group on another, so the leaves are offered directly and each one names the row it came from. THE ENCHANTED WEAPON GRANTS NO BLOCK: its fifteen powers are the WEAPON''s, printed 88-90, split into Weapons of Order and Weapons of Chaos, and they are neither spells nor super abilities nor catalog rows of any kind. They are in the body. SPELL LEVELS AND P.P.E. ARE NOT STATED because this book states neither - decision D5. Capacity is spells per DAY and the index prints a PICK COST in parentheses, so a spell marked (2) or (3) costs two or three of the selections a package grants. Nothing here can deduct that; the counts above are the book''s printed numbers and the parenthetical cost is the player''s to honour, exactly as at the table. STARTING MONEY IS NOT STATED for any of the five sub-types - the magic sections print no financial resources line at all, unlike every other power category - so the class states none rather than borrowing another category''s figure. CIRCLE MAGIC (printed 103-107) IS NOT IMPORTED: protection circles, circles of power and summoning circles are a separate discipline with their own drawing rules and their own costs, available to the wizard alone, and the catalog has no shape for one. Neither are golems and zombies, printed 107."
