## Lore

Magic provides incredible powers and abilities that seem to tap an unknown
energy source, one likely to have otherworldly origin. Exactly what it is, or
where it comes from, is a mystery even to those who wield it. What is known is
that, like any source of power, it can be used for good or for evil.

There are four ways to get mystic powers: an enchanted weapon, an enchanted
talisman, years of study, or a gift bestowed by a creature of magic.

With an **enchanted weapon** or an **enchanted object**, the magic is in the
item and not in the person. Without it the character is an ordinary individual
armed only with his skills and his wits. A weapon is usually aligned to order or
to chaos and works only for a kindred spirit; an object rarely is, so good and
evil use the same talisman indiscriminately. The knowledge an object provides
never changes and can never be increased - its bearer directs the magic and
knows nothing about magic, so he can learn neither spells nor circles.

**Mystic study** is the opposite: the character himself is the caster.
Wizardry taps the fabric of mystic energies and weaves it into a focused force,
the spoken incantation igniting it while the wizard''s will shapes and directs
it. Because those secrets are dangerous, their masters hide them: the power
words are whispered so quietly as to be barely audible, buried in meaningless
phrases, and only the meaningless parts are ever spoken aloud. The magician
casts the same way, but the scope of his art is optical and illusionary. Most
wizards consider him a novice, or a lazy mage who lacked the patience for the
harder work. He is powerful in his own right all the same.

**Mystically bestowed** characters are chosen by the supernatural forces of
order and chaos to champion their cause - usually a very ordinary person whose
moral integrity and emotional state are deemed exactly right. The force appears,
explains that a great gift is coming, gives a speech about the eternal battle
and a pep talk, and then, poof.

## GM Notes

**The weapon''s fifteen powers**, printed 88-90, belong to the weapon rather than
to the character, and they are not in any catalog. They divide into Weapons of
Order and Weapons of Chaos, and the chaos list ends with Portal of Fear, Mystic
Shield, Power of Darkness (impervious to poisons and toxic gases, +2 P.E., +6
Speed, +10% prowl and 1D4x10 S.D.C.), Tongues, and Cloud of Smoke.

**The weapon type**, printed 90 - it must be an ancient hand-held weapon, never
a modern one: 01-10 battle axe, 11-20 spear, 21-32 short sword, 33-45 large
sword, 46-58 staff, 59-70 mace, 71-80 war hammer, 81-90 ball and chain, 91-00
morning star.

**Physical limitations for a bestowed character**, printed 95, entirely at the
player''s option and rather the point of the archetype: 01-20 incapacitated by
disease or accident, one physical skill excluding boxing, wrestling and
gymnastics, all physical attributes 11 or lower; 21-40 old age, 50 + 4D6 years,
two physical skills, P.S., P.P. and P.E. 12 or lower; 41-60 a kid, 10 + 1D6
years, two physical skills excluding boxing and wrestling, no physical attribute
over 14; 61-80 a wimp of any age, no physical skills, every physical attribute
10 or less; 81-00 an invalid confined to a wheelchair, upper-body skills only.

A bestowed character forced to save against the negation of magic saves at +4;
a failed save turns him back into an ordinary person for 1D6 melees, which can
be a long time in a fierce battle.

**Learning more spells** is hard for everyone. A wizard may return to his master
(one month of study for a simple spell, 1D4 months for one marked (2), 2D4 for
one marked (3)), be granted 1D4 spells as a boon by a grateful supernatural
being or high-level wizard - 1D4 months of unbroken study EACH, and a broken
study loses the spell and ends the teaching - or teach himself from ancient
texts, eight months per spell, with a roll that can go badly wrong. A magician
has only his master, or another illusionist willing to share.

Hand to hand combat is not automatic for any of the five and must be selected as
a learned skill; every hero gets two attacks per melee. Casting a spell counts
as one action and takes the place of a hand to hand attack, and a caster may
have more magic attacks than physical ones - it simply means no physical combat
that melee. Magic and physical combat mix freely otherwise.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-magic');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-magic';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-hu-magic-class.sql');
